{
  "id": "COMPOUND:20134 - PROTEIN:5783",
  "verbalization": "Marsdekoiside A is implicated in the biological pathway leading to M19-MEL through multiple indirect routes. The drug acts as a target for Carboxylesterase 2, which in turn is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, a compound that ultimately targets M19-MEL. Similarly, Marsdekoiside A also targets Raji and SNB-78, which are both targeted by the same intermediate compound, reinforcing the connection to M19-MEL. These pathways suggest a potential mechanism where Marsdekoiside A influences downstream targets through a shared intermediate, possibly modulating the activity of the intermediate compound. The evidence supports a hierarchical relationship where Marsdekoiside A's effects are mediated through a common target, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn affects M19-MEL. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Marsdekoiside A in modulating the activity of a key intermediate, thereby influencing M19-MEL.",
